# D) Repack BOOT image (mkbootimg) — worked

## D1. Get mkbootimg tools

```bash
mkdir -p ~/android-tools && cd ~/android-tools
git clone https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/tools/mkbootimg
```

## D2. Extract AP tar + decompress boot

```bash
cd /mnt/DATA/SM-A135F/raw
mkdir -p work_ap && cd work_ap

tar -xvf ../AP_*.tar.md5 boot.img.lz4 dtbo.img.lz4 vbmeta.img.lz4
lz4 -d boot.img.lz4 boot.img

mkdir -p boot_unpack
python3 ~/android-tools/mkbootimg/unpack_bootimg.py --boot_img boot.img --out boot_unpack
```

## D3. Replace kernel + repack (header v2 params yang kamu punya)

> Kernel original non-gzip → pakai `Image` (bukan Image.gz).

```bash
cd /mnt/DATA/SM-A135F/raw/work_ap

cp -f /mnt/DATA/SM-A135F/src/Kernel/arch/arm64/boot/Image boot_unpack/kernel

python3 ~/android-tools/mkbootimg/mkbootimg.py \
  --header_version 2 \
  --os_version 14.0.0 \
  --os_patch_level 2025-11 \
  --pagesize 0x00000800 \
  --base 0x00000000 \
  --kernel_offset 0x10008000 \
  --ramdisk_offset 0x11000000 \
  --second_offset 0x00000000 \
  --tags_offset 0x10000100 \
  --dtb_offset 0x0000000010000000 \
  --board SRPUK09B013 \
  --cmdline "androidboot.hardware=exynos850 androidboot.selinux=enforce loop.max_part=7" \
  --kernel boot_unpack/kernel \
  --ramdisk boot_unpack/ramdisk \
  --dtb boot_unpack/dtb \
  --output boot_manualksu.img

file boot_manualksu.img
```

